 "final_text": "Here's the tie-out for CES Direct, February:\n\n| | Amount |\n|---|---|\n| **Parent AR balance** (our books, IC-001) | **$76,500** |\n| **CES-recorded balance** (their intercompany schedule, 2/28) | **$54,000** |\n| **Difference** | **$22,500** |\n\n**What's behind it:** Three intercompany invoices make up our $76,500 AR from CES Direct \u2014 ICINV-01 ($30,000, Q4 shared services, booked 1/10), ICINV-02 ($24,000, January inventory transfer, booked 2/5), and ICINV-03 ($22,500, February management fee, dated 2/27). CES's own schedule only shows the first two as booked ($54,000). ICINV-03 didn't reach CES until 3/1 and won't post on their side until March \u2014 confirmed by Dana Kim's 3/1 email flagging it as the one in-transit item. So the full $22,500 gap is a timing/cutoff difference, not a dispute or error, and it self-resolves in March.\n\nSubmitted via `submit_answer`.",
